# pdfdebug-server config - env vars only, no flags and no config file
# (this is a wails v3 server-mode default, confirmed by actually running
# the binary - pdfdebug itself sets no overrides of its own).
#
# SECURITY: confirmed by research - this server has NO authentication of
# any kind. Defaults to binding localhost only, which is why that default
# is kept as-is here rather than widened. If you change WAILS_SERVER_HOST
# to something reachable off-box, put it behind your own auth (reverse
# proxy, VPN, whatever) - nothing in pdfdebug itself will do that for you.
#
# Must be `export`ed, not just set - OpenRC sources this file into the
# init script's own shell, it doesn't `set -a` it, so an unexported var
# here never reaches the process start-stop-daemon execs (same lesson
# learned the hard way on isms.confd earlier in this repo's history).
#export WAILS_SERVER_HOST="localhost"
#export WAILS_SERVER_PORT="8080"
